@startuml Preciazo_DB_Community_Price_Verification

title Preciazo - Community Price Verification Database Diagram

hide circle
skinparam linetype ortho

entity price_observations {
    * id : BIGINT <<PK>>
    --
    catalog_entry_id : BIGINT <<REF>>
    discrepancy_id : BIGINT <<FK>>
    observer_id : BIGINT <<REF>>
    observed_price : DECIMAL
    currency : VARCHAR
    observed_at : TIMESTAMP
    source : VARCHAR
}

entity price_discrepancies {
    * id : BIGINT <<PK>>
    --
    catalog_entry_id : BIGINT <<REF>>
    reporter_id : BIGINT <<REF>>
    expected_price : DECIMAL
    observed_price : DECIMAL
    currency : VARCHAR
    reported_at : TIMESTAMP
    version : BIGINT
    confidence_score : DECIMAL <<NULLABLE>>
    status : VARCHAR
}

entity verification_votes {
    * id : BIGINT <<PK>>
    --
    discrepancy_id : BIGINT <<FK>>
    voter_id : BIGINT <<REF>>
    vote_type : VARCHAR
    created_at : TIMESTAMP
}

entity trust_profiles {
    * id : BIGINT <<PK>>
    --
    user_id : BIGINT <<REF, UQ>>
    score : DECIMAL
    level : VARCHAR
}

price_discrepancies ||--o{ verification_votes
price_discrepancies ||--|{ price_observations : supported by

note right of price_observations
  catalog_entry_id belongs to
  Catalog and Pricing.
end note


note right of verification_votes
  UNIQUE(discrepancy_id, voter_id).
  vote_type is CONFIRM or REJECT; immutable after submission.
  Proposed: voter differs from reporter; report must be OPEN.
  Duplicate votes do not produce another vote event.
end note

note right of price_discrepancies
  US28: status is OPEN, UNDER_REVIEW, ACCEPTED or REJECTED.
  Anomalous or unchecked reports are retained as UNDER_REVIEW.
  Initial anomaly screening completes in the report transaction.
  version supports optimistic concurrency; terminal states do not reopen.
  confidence_score remains unset until a confidence rule is configured.
  Formula and acceptance/rejection thresholds are pending decisions.
  TS07: index (reporter_id, catalog_entry_id, reported_at).
  Reject a repeat report within 60 seconds; enforce atomically per buyer/offer.
  A time-window check is not a permanent UNIQUE(buyer, offer) constraint.
end note

note bottom of price_observations
  At least one observation per discrepancy.
  Nonnegative prices; expected and observed prices use the same currency.
  The observation belongs to the discrepancy's catalog offer.
end note

entity discrepancy_reviews {
    * id : BIGINT <<PK>>
    --
    discrepancy_id : BIGINT <<FK, UQ>>
    reviewer_id : BIGINT <<REF>>
    decision : VARCHAR
    reason : VARCHAR
    reviewed_at : TIMESTAMP
}

entity processed_verification_events {
    * id : BIGINT <<PK>>
    --
    event_id : VARCHAR
    handler_name : VARCHAR
    discrepancy_id : BIGINT <<FK>>
    processed_at : TIMESTAMP
}

price_discrepancies ||--o| discrepancy_reviews
price_discrepancies ||--o{ processed_verification_events

note right of discrepancy_reviews
  One final human review per report; decision is ACCEPT or REJECT.
  Reviewer requires price-reports:resolve; reason is mandatory.
  Report must be UNDER_REVIEW; review and status change are atomic.
  reviewer_id references Identity and Access by identifier only.
end note

note right of processed_verification_events
  UNIQUE(event_id, handler_name).
  Marker and domain mutation commit together or roll back together.
  Domain event identity is distinct from the generated BIGINT row id.
end note

@enduml
